<http://data.silknow.org/object/26462196-2028-3e05-b677-2162ecc4cec0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Design: silk printed with the game; edged with green silk turned and sewn by hand along the two short sides.  \nNo. of squares: 84\nSquares illustrated: 84\nSquare numbering: 1 to 84\nSquares titled: all\nSubject of starting square: The Infant\nSubject of ending square: memorial monument with an urn on the shoulders of women who stand on a column and steps which are surrounded by four figures.  On the column is a tablet showing the portrait bust of a man  above the words ML LEOPOLD/HERvBRAUNS/GEB1752GEST85 (probably Leopold, Son/Lord/Prince? of Brunswick, born 1752 died 1785)."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/26462196-2028-3e05-b677-2162ecc4cec0> .

<http://data.silknow.org/production/312bbb6a-36d2-32bf-b38d-a94be71dcda6/activity/1>
